 Bind the channel to an agent via that agent's `channels` list.

+### Group-only agents on one Signal account
+
+Set `group_only = true` and list each agent's group in `group_ids` to reject
+DMs before agent or approval processing. Bind each channel alias to one agent.
+This is mutually exclusive with `dm_only`; both new options default to false.
+
+On exactly one enabled alias for an account, optionally set
+`dm_unsupported_notice = true`. Allowlisted senders who DM that account receive
+"DMs aren't supported. Please use an agent's group." The DM is never dispatched
+to an agent. Notices are limited to one attempt per sender per five minutes,
+shared by clones of that channel, with a bounded in-memory cache. Restarting
+resets the cache. Failed sends are also rate limited. Configure the notice
+alias's external peers to include everyone who should receive this notice;
+unauthorized senders, stories, receipts, and empty-text messages are ignored.
+Enabling notices on multiple aliases for the same account fails validation.
+
+```toml
+[channels.signal.media]
+enabled = true
+http_url = "http://127.0.0.1:8686"
+account = "+15551234567"
+group_ids = ["<media-group-id>"]
+group_only = true
+dm_unsupported_notice = true
+
+[agents.media]
+channels = ["signal.media"]
+# Also configure this agent's model_provider, risk_profile, and runtime_profile.
+
+[peer_groups.media-members]
+channel = "signal.media"
+agents = ["media"]
+external_peers = ["+15557654321"]
+```
+
 ## Start and check

 Start the daemon first, then start ZeroClaw channels:
